# NOTE: a bare pattern like `.next` only matches at the context root —
# Docker does not recurse. Every directory that exists per-workspace
# (build caches, node_modules, env files) needs the `**/` prefix or the
# builder stage's `COPY . .` drags the host's copy into the image:
# stale .next caches poison `next build`, macOS-native node_modules
# shadow the Linux deps installed by `npm ci`, and .env.local would
# bake local secrets into the layer.
.git
.github
**/.next
**/node_modules
**/.turbo
**/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
**/coverage
docs
apps/mcp-server/*
!apps/mcp-server/package.json
supabase
*.md
!README.md
# No .env file belongs in an image. Runtime secrets arrive via
# docker-compose's env_file; the web build's NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are
# copied explicitly from apps/web/env/next-public.production (a
# deliberately committed, secret-free file that this rule doesn't match).
**/.env*
!**/.env.local.example
Dockerfile
Dockerfile.api
docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore
.vscode
.idea
.claude
